Static inspection confirms the key structural distinction: C1/C2 are scored as differences, so a common output bias cancels; C3 is added as an absolute interaction term. The neutral targets are exactly zero, regularization is zero, and only the pairwise heads have gauge centering. I’m now binding the empirical test to one route—C3, the route whose bias can actually survive deployment—and one seed, using five stored training anchors and five fixed evaluation anchors.
